$PC$ and $PQ$ are tangents to the circle, centre $O$, and $PNB$ is a secant, with $N$ the nearer intersection point.
$PN = 4\text{ cm}$ and $NB = 21\text{ cm}$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.26]
\usetikzlibrary{calc, decorations.markings}
\tikzset{tickmark/.style={postaction={decorate, decoration={markings, mark=at position 0.5 with {\draw[black] (0pt,-4pt) -- (0pt,4pt);}}}}}
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (P) at (14.5,0);
\coordinate (C) at (7.603,7.241);
\coordinate (Q) at (7.603,-7.241);
\coordinate (N) at (10.5,0);
\coordinate (F) at (-10.5,0);
\draw (O) circle (10.5);
\fill (O) circle (1.5pt);
\node[above] at (O) {$O$};
\draw[tickmark] (P) -- (C);
\draw[tickmark] (P) -- (Q);
\draw (P) -- (F);
\fill (N) circle (1.5pt);
\node[right] at (P) {$P$};
\node[above right] at (C) {$C$};
\node[below right] at (Q) {$Q$};
\node[below] at (N) {$N$};
\node[left] at (F) {$B$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Find the length of $PQ$.

$T$ is the point of contact of tangent $TP$ to the circle, centre $O$, with radius $8\text{ cm}$ and $OP = 17\text{ cm}$ (so $PT = 15\text{ cm}$ by Pythagoras' theorem).
$TA$ is a chord, and $B$ is a point on the circle.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.32]
\usetikzlibrary{calc, angles, quotes}
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (T) at (0,8);
\coordinate (L) at (-2,8);
\coordinate (R) at (15.5,8);
\coordinate (P) at (15,8);
\coordinate (A) at (6.632,-4.474);
\coordinate (B) at (-7.518,-2.736);
\draw (O) circle (8);
\fill (O) circle (1.5pt);
\node[below] at (O) {$O$};
\draw (L) -- (R);
\draw (O) -- (T);
\draw (O) -- (P);
\draw (T) -- (A);
\draw (T) -- (B);
\draw (A) -- (B);
\node[above] at (T) {$T$};
\node[right] at (P) {$P$};
\node[right] at (A) {$A$};
\node[left] at (B) {$B$};
\coordinate (ta) at ($(T)!0.3cm!(O)$);
\coordinate (tp) at ($(T)!0.3cm!(P)$);
\draw (ta) -- ($(ta)+(tp)-(T)$) -- (tp);
\pic[draw, angle radius=1.1cm] {angle=A--T--R};
\node[anchor=south west, xshift=36pt, yshift=14pt] (anglelabel) at (T) {$62^{\circ}$};
\draw[->] (anglelabel.south west) -- ($(T)+(27pt,-16pt)$);
\pic[draw, "$y$", angle radius=1cm, angle eccentricity=2] {angle=A--B--T};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Find the value of $y$.

$PC$ is a tangent and $PNB$ is a secant drawn from the external point $P$ to the circle, centre $O$, with $N$ the nearer intersection point.
$PN = 8\text{ cm}$ and $NB = 10\text{ cm}$.
The tangent-chord angle between $PC$ and chord $CN$ is approximately $33.69^{\circ}$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.39]
\usetikzlibrary{calc, angles, quotes}
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (P) at (13,0);
\coordinate (C) at (1.923,4.615);
\coordinate (N) at (5,0);
\coordinate (F) at (-5,0);
\draw (O) circle (5);
\fill (O) circle (1.5pt);
\node[above] at (O) {$O$};
\draw (P) -- (C);
\draw (P) -- (F);
\draw (C) -- (N);
\draw (C) -- (F);
\fill (N) circle (1.5pt);
\node[below] at (P) {$P$};
\node[above right] at (C) {$C$};
\node[anchor=north west, xshift=4pt, yshift=-4pt] at (N) {$N$};
\node[left] at (F) {$B$};
\pic[draw, angle radius=0.4cm] {angle=N--C--P};
\node[anchor=south west, xshift=30pt, yshift=14pt] (anglelabel) at (C) {$\approx 33.69^{\circ}$};
\draw[->] (anglelabel.south west) -- ($(C)+(8pt,-10pt)$);
\pic[draw, "$y$", angle radius=0.5cm, angle eccentricity=2] {angle=N--F--C};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
(a) Find the length of $PC$.
(b) Find the value of $y$ to 2 decimal places.

A climber at $P$ is attached to two ropes $PC$ and $PQ$, each tangent to a circular cliff ledge, centre $O$.
A third rope $PNB$ crosses the ledge as a secant, with $N$ the nearer intersection point.
$PN = 2\text{ m}$ and $NB = 30\text{ m}$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.22]
\usetikzlibrary{calc, decorations.markings}
\tikzset{tickmark/.style={postaction={decorate, decoration={markings, mark=at position 0.5 with {\draw[black] (0pt,-4pt) -- (0pt,4pt);}}}}}
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (P) at (17,0);
\coordinate (C) at (13.235,7.059);
\coordinate (Q) at (13.235,-7.059);
\coordinate (N) at (15,0);
\coordinate (F) at (-15,0);
\draw (O) circle (15);
\fill (O) circle (1.5pt);
\node[above] at (O) {$O$};
\draw[tickmark] (P) -- (C);
\draw[tickmark] (P) -- (Q);
\draw (P) -- (F);
\fill (N) circle (1.5pt);
\node[right] at (P) {$P$};
\node[above right] at (C) {$C$};
\node[below right] at (Q) {$Q$};
\node[below] at (N) {$N$};
\node[left] at (F) {$B$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Find the length of rope $PQ$.

$PT$ and $PQ$ are tangents to the circle, centre $O$, with $PT = PQ = 10\text{ cm}$ and $\angle TPQ = 40^{\circ}$.
$C$ is a point on the circle in the alternate segment for chord $TQ$.
A secant $PAB$ is also drawn from $P$, with $A$ the nearer intersection point, and $PA = 8\text{ cm}$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.5]
\usetikzlibrary{calc, decorations.markings, angles, quotes}
\tikzset{tickmark/.style={postaction={decorate, decoration={markings, mark=at position 0.5 with {\draw[black] (0pt,-4pt) -- (0pt,4pt);}}}}}
\coordinate (P) at (0,0);
\coordinate (O) at (10.642,0);
\coordinate (T) at (9.397,3.42);
\coordinate (Q) at (9.397,-3.42);
\draw (O) circle (3.64);
\fill (O) circle (1.5pt);
\node[below] at (O) {$O$};
\draw[tickmark] (P) -- (T);
\draw[tickmark] (P) -- (Q);
\draw (T) -- (Q);
\node[left] at (P) {$P$};
\node[above] at (T) {$T$};
\node[below] at (Q) {$Q$};
\coordinate (C) at (14.282,0);
\draw (T) -- (C) -- (Q);
\node[right] at (C) {$C$};
\coordinate (A) at (7.706,2.151);
\coordinate (B) at (12.040,3.361);
\draw (P) -- (B);
\fill (A) circle (1.5pt);
\fill (B) circle (1.5pt);
\node[above left] at (A) {$A$};
\node[above right] at (B) {$B$};
\pic[draw, "$40^{\circ}$", angle radius=0.4cm, angle eccentricity=2] {angle=Q--P--T};
\pic[draw, "$x$", angle radius=0.4cm, angle eccentricity=2] {angle=P--T--Q};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
(a) Find the value of $x = \angle PTQ$.
(b) Find the length $PB$ of the secant $PAB$.
